{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Phase 2 test contract frozen before repair.\n\nauthoritative_contract: user requirement that supported tests run locally and in CI; AGENTS.md portability/failure-investigation contracts; existing fixtures promise successful bare-remote initialization.\ntrigger_preconditions: real temporary bare repositories; process-only GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL containing safe.bareRepository=explicit; GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1; no host/global/system mutation.\nproduction_path: real pytest fixture setup for concurrency, prepare-reclaim, and reclaim-history through their actual Git subprocess helpers.\ntest_tier: subprocess integration with real Git repositories and refs; a unit mock cannot exercise Git protected bare-repository discovery.\nobservable_postcondition: the three actual fixture-backed nodes pass under strict policy and under an isolated default-policy control; exact upkeep pins and HEAD refs remain correct; nonexistent explicit repositories still fail with rc 128.\nci_gate: the held-out integration node is collected by the normal pytest integration/default matrix.\nnegative_control: identical fixture nodes under isolated default Git config also pass.\ncollateral_invariants: worktree helper behavior, gc.autoDetach/maintenance.autoDetach/receive.autogc=false, HEAD=refs/heads/tickets, --no-hardlinks, fail-fast subprocess checks, and genuine Git errors remain unchanged.\n\nFinal-form held-out oracle was observed RED before repair: 1 failed; its nested real-fixture probe produced exactly three setup errors. Concurrency failed at git config gc.autoDetach false in remote.git (rc 128); prepare-reclaim and reclaim-history failed at git -C source.git symbolic-ref HEAD refs/heads/tickets (rc 128). The test itself was collected and executed, with failure at the strict-policy postcondition rather than import/collection. The oracle has now been removed from the worktree before blind fixing."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787097875404264001,"uuid":"4d62dd93-b882-469f-846d-e611b0f81594"}